   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>
                        <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">Scrivo a lungo pazienza spiegherò</seg>
                    </p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">
                                <choice>
                                    <sic>Gosce</sic>
                                    <corr>Joyce</corr>
                                </choice>
                            </name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">According to dates and times stamped on this telegram, it was sent by JJ from Trieste on 5 June 1920 at “13.35” (1.35 p.m.), and was received in Sirmione on 6 June at “10.25” (a.m.).</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">
                    <p>“Will write fully patience will explain.” JJ’s long letter to Pound dated 5 June 1920 set forth multiple, involved reasons for his not being able to travel to Sirmione at the present time (see <rs type="letter" key="L_68611">JJ to Pound, 5 June 1920</rs>, notes); and his telegram to Pound dated 31 May 1920 indicated that he had earlier been held up by a railway strike (see <rs type="letter" key="L_68607">JJ telegram to Pound, 31 May 1920</rs>, notes). Another long letter written by JJ, most likely also on 31 May 1920 (but misdated by Ellmann as 5 June 1920), elaborated on the railway strike and a train accident (in which JJ was not involved) that had been the initial obstacles to his setting forth (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">LII</name> 467–69; <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Pound/Joyce</name> 167-69).</p>
                    <p>Despite all the real and imagined setbacks, JJ did arrive in Desenzano, the railway stop a few miles from Sirmione, with his son <name type="person" key="joyc05">Giorgio</name>, on the night of 8 June 1920, and spent two days with Pound and his wife <name type="person" key="poun86">Dorothy</name> in Sirmione (for full accounts, see <rs type="letter" key="L_68605">JJ telegram to Pound, 26 May 1920</rs>, notes; <rs type="letter" key="L_68611">JJ letter to Pound, 5 June 1920</rs>, notes).</p>
                </note>
            </div>
      </body>
